# test/fixtures/website-section-kinds.json is a declared BYTE-IDENTICAL copy shared
# with arion-api (its source of truth is lib/websiteBuilder/sectionSchema.js), and a
# test in each repo asserts the two files match byte for byte. core.autocrlf=true on
# a Windows machine hands a fresh checkout CRLF here and LF there, which fails that
# assertion for a reason that has nothing to do with the seam. LF, everywhere, always
# — the same pin arion-api already puts on scripts/_tools.mjs.
test/fixtures/website-section-kinds.json text eol=lf
# test/fixtures/email-render-cases.json and landing-render-cases.json are the same
# kind of declared byte-identical copy, shared with LUMEN-API: the Portal renders
# each case with src/builder/adapters/{email,landing}/*Render.ts and the API renders
# it with src/lib/{builderEmailRender,landingRender}.js, and the two are only
# provably the same renderer while the two files are the same bytes.
test/fixtures/email-render-cases.json text eol=lf
test/fixtures/landing-render-cases.json text eol=lf
# src/pages/oliver/look/presets.ts is the Portal's copy of the customer portal's
# src/look/presets.ts (CUSTOMER_PORTAL_LOOK_SCOPE_2026-09-25 §5.1); a test in each
# repo asserts the two are byte-identical. Same pin, same reason as above.
src/pages/oliver/look/presets.ts text eol=lf
